    "sentence_translations": [
      "On “菜”",
      "",
      "In Chinese, the word “菜” is very interesting.",
      "We can use it to refer to the “菜” that we eat, and we can also use it to refer to people.",
      "",
      "If someone says “they are not my ‘菜’”, it means that the person speaking does not like that person.",
      "Here, the term “菜” refers to “someone you like”. You can use it like this: “Although he is nice, he’s not my ‘菜’.”",
      "",
      "If someone is not good at something, we can say, “He is very ‘菜’.”",
      "Sometimes you will hear, “He’s too ‘菜’ at playing games.”",
      "Here, the term ‘菜’ means that this person is not good at playing games.",
      "",
      "Sometimes, people will also say “菜鸟”, which refers to a novice.",
      "We can say, “I just learned how to drive, and today is my first day on the road. I’m a ‘菜鸟’.”",
      "",
      "These usages make the word “菜” very interesting."
    ]
  }
